>
  <h1>Verifying Credentials</h1>
  <p class="docs-hero-sub">
    Validate W3C Verifiable Credentials with the <code>VCVerifier</code> class.
    Check signatures, expiration, issuer identity, and detect tampering.
  </p>

  <h2>Two verification modes</h2>
  <p>The SDK supports two ways to verify a credential:</p>

  <ul style="color: var(--docs-text-muted); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 2; padding-left: 1.5rem;">
    <li><strong style="color: var(--docs-text);">verifyWithKey</strong> — you supply the public key directly. No network calls.</li>
    <li><strong style="color: var(--docs-text);">verify</strong> — resolves the issuer's DID to fetch the public key automatically.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>verifyWithKey</h2>
  <p>Use when you already know the issuer's public key:</p>

  <CodeBlock lang="TypeScript" title="Verify with known key">
<Fragment set:html={`<span class="c-kw">import</span> <span class="c-br">{</span> VCVerifier <span class="c-br">}</span> <span class="c-kw">from</span> <span class="c-str">'@attestto-com/vc-sdk'</span>

<span class="c-kw">const</span> verifier = <span class="c-kw">new</span> <span class="c-fn">VCVerifier</span>()

<span class="c-kw">const</span> result = <span class="c-kw">await</span> verifier.<span class="c-fn">verifyWithKey</span>(vc, publicKey, <span class="c-str">'Ed25519'</span>, <span class="c-br">{</span>
  expectedType: <span class="c-str">'ProfessionalLicense'</span>,
  expectedIssuer: <span class="c-str">'did:web:issuer.example.com'</span>,
  checkExpiration: <span class="c-kw">true</span>,
<span class="c-br">}</span>)

console.<span class="c-fn">log</span>(result.valid)   <span class="c-cm">// true or false</span>
console.<span class="c-fn">log</span>(result.checks)  <span class="c-cm">// detailed check results</span>
console.<span class="c-fn">log</span>(result.errors)  <span class="c-cm">// array of failure reasons</span>`} />
  </CodeBlock>

  <h2>verify (with DID resolver)</h2>
  <p>Use when you want the SDK to resolve the issuer's DID document and extract the public key:</p>

  <CodeBlock lang="TypeScript" title="Verify with DID resolution">
<Fragment set:html={`<span class="c-kw">import</span> <span class="c-br">{</span> VCVerifier <span class="c-br">}</span> <span class="c-kw">from</span> <span class="c-str">'@attestto-com/vc-sdk'</span>

<span class="c-kw">const</span> verifier = <span class="c-kw">new</span> <span class="c-fn">VCVerifier</span>(<span class="c-br">{</span>
  resolver: myDidResolver, <span class="c-cm">// implements DID resolution</span>
<span class="c-br">}</span>)

<span class="c-kw">const</span> result = <span class="c-kw">await</span> verifier.<span class="c-fn">verify</span>(vc, <span class="c-br">{</span>
  expectedType: <span class="c-str">'DrivingLicense'</span>,
  checkExpiration: <span class="c-kw">true</span>,
  checkStatus: <span class="c-kw">true</span>,
<span class="c-br">}</span>)

<span class="c-kw">if</span> (result.valid) <span class="c-br">{</span>
  console.<span class="c-fn">log</span>(<span class="c-str">'Credential is valid'</span>)
<span class="c-br">}</span> <span class="c-kw">else</span> <span class="c-br">{</span>
  console.<span class="c-fn">log</span>(<span class="c-str">'Errors:'</span>, result.errors)
<span class="c-br">}</span>`} />
  </CodeBlock>

  <h2>VerifyOptions</h2>

  <CodeBlock lang="TypeScript" title="VerifyOptions interface">
<Fragment set:html={`<span class="c-kw">interface</span> <span class="c-typ">VerifyOptions</span> <span class="c-br">{</span>
  expectedType<span class="c-op">?</span>: <span class="c-typ">string</span>      <span class="c-cm">// Assert credential contains this type</span>
  expectedIssuer<span class="c-op">?</span>: <span class="c-typ">string</span>    <span class="c-cm">// Assert issuer DID matches</span>
  expectedContext<span class="c-op">?</span>: <span class="c-typ">string</span>   <span class="c-cm">// Assert @context includes this URI</span>
  checkExpiration<span class="c-op">?</span>: <span class="c-typ">boolean</span>  <span class="c-cm">// Check expirationDate against now (default: true)</span>
  checkStatus<span class="c-op">?</span>: <span class="c-typ">boolean</span>      <span class="c-cm">// Check credentialStatus endpoint (default: false)</span>
<span class="c-br">}</span>`} />
  </CodeBlock>

  <h2>VerificationResult</h2>

  <CodeBlock lang="TypeScript" title="VerificationResult interface">
<Fragment set:html={`<span class="c-kw">interface</span> <span class="c-typ">VerificationResult</span> <span class="c-br">{</span>
  valid: <span class="c-typ">boolean</span>              <span class="c-cm">// Overall pass/fail</span>
  checks: <span class="c-typ">CheckResult</span>[]      <span class="c-cm">// Individual check outcomes</span>
  errors: <span class="c-typ">string</span>[]            <span class="c-cm">// Failure reasons (empty if valid)</span>
  warnings: <span class="c-typ">string</span>[]          <span class="c-cm">// Non-fatal issues</span>
<span class="c-br">}</span>`} />
  </CodeBlock>

  <h2>Verification checks</h2>
  <p>The verifier runs these checks in order. Each produces a <code>CheckResult</code> entry:</p>

  <ul style="color: var(--docs-text-muted); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 2; padding-left: 1.5rem;">
    <li><strong style="color: var(--docs-text);">structure.context</strong> — <code>@context</code> includes the W3C credentials URI.</li>
    <li><strong style="color: var(--docs-text);">structure.type</strong> — <code>type</code> array includes <code>VerifiableCredential</code>.</li>
    <li><strong style="color: var(--docs-text);">structure.issuer</strong> — <code>issuer</code> field is present and is a valid DID.</li>
    <li><strong style="color: var(--docs-text);">structure.subject</strong> — <code>credentialSubject</code> is present.</li>
    <li><strong style="color: var(--docs-text);">structure.issuanceDate</strong> — <code>issuanceDate</code> is a valid ISO 8601 timestamp.</li>
    <li><strong style="color: var(--docs-text);">proof.signature</strong> — cryptographic signature is valid against the public key.</li>
    <li><strong style="color: var(--docs-text);">proof.algorithm</strong> — proof type matches the expected algorithm.</li>
    <li><strong style="color: var(--docs-text);">temporal.expiration</strong> — credential has not expired (if <code>checkExpiration</code> is enabled).</li>
    <li><strong style="color: var(--docs-text);">temporal.notBefore</strong> — current time is after issuance date.</li>
    <li><strong style="color: var(--docs-text);">policy.type</strong> — credential type matches <code>expectedType</code> (if provided).</li>
    <li><strong style="color: var(--docs-text);">policy.issuer</strong> — issuer DID matches <code>expectedIssuer</code> (if provided).</li>
    <li><strong style="color: var(--docs-text);">policy.context</strong> — context matches <code>expectedContext</code> (if provided).</li>
    <li><strong style="color: var(--docs-text);">status.revocation</strong> — credential is not revoked (if <code>checkStatus</code> is enabled).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Tamper detection</h2>
  <p>If any field in the credential is modified after signing, the signature check fails:</p>

  <CodeBlock lang="TypeScript" title="Detecting tampering">
<Fragment set:html={`<span class="c-cm">// Tamper with the credential</span>
<span class="c-kw">const</span> tampered = <span class="c-br">{</span> ...vc <span class="c-br">}</span>
tampered.credentialSubject = <span class="c-br">{</span>
  ...tampered.credentialSubject,
  profession: <span class="c-str">'Brain Surgeon'</span>, <span class="c-cm">// was 'Civil Engineer'</span>
<span class="c-br">}</span>

<span class="c-kw">const</span> result = <span class="c-kw">await</span> verifier.<span class="c-fn">verifyWithKey</span>(tampered, publicKey, <span class="c-str">'Ed25519'</span>)

console.<span class="c-fn">log</span>(result.valid)    <span class="c-cm">// false</span>
console.<span class="c-fn">log</span>(result.errors)   <span class="c-cm">// ['proof.signature: Signature verification failed']</span>`} />
  </CodeBlock>

  <Callout type="warning">
    <strong>Always verify before trusting.</strong> A credential is just a JSON object until
    its proof is verified. Never extract claims from an unverified credential.
  </Callout>

